  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRESI OKDD SERACOM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to &#x2018;strengthen the resilience of poor and vulnerable communities affected by the security crisis and the effects of climate change in Burkina Faso&#x2019; through the following specific objective: to improve the living conditions of vulnerable local communities in 11 municipalities in the Centre-North and Sahel regions. To achieve this, a theory of change (ToC) is structured around approaches that will enable the consortium to: (i) restore livelihoods through non-productive and productive social protection activities. This will mainly involve the distribution of small ruminants, village-based poultry farming and the distribution of agro-pastoral inputs. It will also aim to protect livelihoods by strengthening productive capacities through the development of agro-pastoral zones, the rehabilitation of degraded land, the integration of climate scenarios into Communal Development Plans (CDPs) and the distribution of agro-pastoral inputs. These actions will contribute to strengthening and protecting livelihoods as well as the productive capacities of vulnerable households, including internally displaced persons. (ii) Furthermore, the use of productive social safety nets to protect livelihoods, as well as labour-intensive works (LIW), which will be carried out in collaboration with the municipalities, will provide a source of financial resources to strengthen the financial capacities of beneficiaries. These LIW activities offer temporary rural employment opportunities to displaced persons and communities. The beneficiaries of these activities (productive and labour-intensive social networks) will be organised both upstream and downstream of the activities to enable them to make good use of the resources they receive. Adopting this strategy will enable them to strengthen their financial capacity in the medium term and integrate into local economic circuits. (iii) Furthermore, the consortium will work in collaboration with the municipalities to establish and revitalise functional, high-quality municipal social services, through support for the provision of high-quality human and material resources. This prerequisite will enable the creation of a single, reliable social register of people&#x2019;s vulnerability at the level of each municipality, which the consortium will use to implement non-productive social safety nets for vulnerable people, in order to strengthen social protection for vulnerable households and people with low productive capacity within their respective municipalities.&#xa0; Given the context, particular emphasis will be placed on conflict sensitivity through the &#x2018;Do no harm&#x2019; approach to prevent conflicts arising from the implementation of project activities.</narrative>
  </description>
